# Files under 3rdparty/bishengir/ are produced on Windows (core.autocrlf=true here)
# but executed on Linux. Without these rules git checks out CRLF copies of the .sh
# files, and bash fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" or stray \r in output.
*.sh     -text
*.patch  -text
*.npuir  -text

# The prebuilt compiler is a 45.8 MB binary; keep it out of diff/merge machinery.
*.tar.gz binary
